# Phase 0 — The Instrumentation Forge

Before any sieve code exists, we build the **measurement and verification instruments** that every later phase is judged by. Phase 0 has one law: **you may not optimize what you cannot measure, and you may not trust what you cannot verify.**

## 0.1 — System Design: The Instrument Stack

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    PHASE 0 INSTRUMENT STACK                      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                  │
│  CPU CANARY ──── fixed-work L1-resident probe ──► frequency      │
│  MEM CANARY ──── 8MiB streaming probe ─────────► DRAM bandwidth  │
│  PER-CORE SURVEY ─ pinned identical work/core ─► throughput      │
│                                                  vector (big:little)│
│  HEATSOAK ────── all-core load + live derate ──► thermal curve   │
│  ORACLE STACK ── 3 interlocked truth layers ───► correctness     │
│  BENCHREF ────── canary-normalized externals ──► honest baseline │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Truth interlock triangle:
   OEIS A006880 (literature) ⟷ trial division (ours) ⟷ primecount (Walisch)
   Each layer independently verifies the other two.
```

**Instrument contracts:**

| Instrument | Contract | Failure mode it kills |
|---|---|---|
| CpuCanary | Identical instruction stream every invocation; 8KiB L1-resident data; **serial dependency chain** (xor→cnt→add) so ILP cannot mask frequency; checksum consumed via `black_box` | "30B/sec" benchmarks that silently measured a throttled core |
| Pinning | Every measurement pinned via `sched_setaffinity` — Android migrates tasks between A76/A55, which *destroys* frequency signals | Canary reading 50% slow because the scheduler moved us to a little core, mistaken as "throttling" |
| Survey | Solo rate + all-core rate per core → **contention factor** (Σsolo ≠ all-core, always) | Naive "8 cores = 8× throughput" planning |
| Oracle tiers | T1 exhaustive/boundary → T2 mid → T3 literature constants. Candidates declare `max_x`; full mode mandatory for the gate | The seive.md disease: small tests pass, big-x lies |
| Mutation gate | 5 known-bad implementations must ALL be caught; an oracle that can't detect injected defects is theater | Trusting an untested test suite |
| Records | Every run → JSON with env snapshot (loadavg, battery, topology, rustc) into `bench/records/` | Unrecorded benchmarks = folklore |

**Spec amendment** (log in file_structure.md): new crate `titan-bench` (canary/survey/hygiene/records). `titan-oracle` stays **fully independent** — zero shared code with anything it verifies, including utilities. The oracle must not inherit bugs from the things it judges.

---

